@.str.23083 = private unnamed_addr constant [352 x i8] c"'raw' is a prefix on function and struct declarations only \E2\80\94 'raw @ name \E2\80\A6' says that a caller must vouch for what the function requires, so only an 'unsafe' function may call it; 'raw : Name { \E2\80\A6 }' seals a struct whose fields carry an invariant. It has no meaning on an import, trait or FFI declaration (a foreign function takes 'unsafe & \E2\80\A6')\00"
@.str.23084 = private unnamed_addr constant [197 x i8] c"'simd' is a prefix on function declarations only \E2\80\94 it selects CPU-dispatched code generation for an '@' declaration, and has no meaning on a const, struct, enum, import, trait or FFI declaration\00"
@.str.23085 = private unnamed_addr constant [317 x i8] c"'pub' has no meaning on a '$' import \E2\80\94 an import inlines another file's declarations and defines no symbol of its own, so there is nothing to export. Mark the declarations in the imported file instead. (Note that a file enters strict visibility at its first 'pub': if this prefix was meant to do that, it did not.)\00"
@.str.23086 = private unnamed_addr constant [185 x i8] c"'inline' is a prefix on function declarations only \E2\80\94 it puts LLVM's 'alwaysinline' on an '@' definition, and has no meaning on a const, struct, enum, import, trait or FFI declaration\00"
@.str.23087 = private unnamed_addr constant [178 x i8] c"'inline' and 'simd' cannot both be applied to one function \E2\80\94 'simd' replaces the function with a CPU-dispatching stub, which is exactly the opaque call 'inline' asks to remove\00"
